About us
Entravel is a member’s club for discounted luxury travel and whitelabel hotel platform provider focusing on the crypto industry, backed by VCs and prominent European founders. Our hotel product is incredibly strong; we offer more than one million properties, and our rates are amongst the lowest in the world. In fact, on most 5* hotels you won’t find a platform with lower rates than Entravel.

Your role
We are looking for a Data Engineer to automate and scale high-volume data workflows, with a strong focus on hotel and room mapping across multiple data sources.
This is an ownership-heavy role: you will take full responsibility for turning a manual, repetitive process into a reliable, scalable system and ensuring it runs correctly in production.

What you’ll do
Own the end-to-end automation of hotel and room mapping workflows;
Take responsibility for delivery, correctness, and reliability of the mapping outputs;
Design and build data pipelines (ingestion → transformation → output);
Translate manual mapping logic into scalable systems;
Implement rule-based and fuzzy matching techniques for entity resolution;
Leverage LLMs to improve mapping accuracy, classification, and edge-case handling;
Normalize and clean inconsistent, messy real-world data;
Build monitoring, validation, and retry mechanisms;
Continuously improve pipeline performance and mapping accuracy.

Ownership & responsibility
You own the mapping system in production;
You are responsible for data quality, accuracy, and failure handling;
You proactively identify gaps, edge cases, and inefficiencies;
You define and evolve the mapping logic and data model;
You ensure issues are detected, debugged, and resolved quickly;
You drive the reduction of manual work and operational overhead.

What we’re looking for
3–6 years of experience in data engineering or similar roles;
Strong Python and SQL;
Experience building pipelines from scratch;
Experience working with messy, third-party, or unstructured data;
Experience with entity matching / deduplication / normalization;
Hands-on experience using LLMs in production workflows;
Strong sense of ownership: you take responsibility for outcomes.

Nice to have
Experience with Rust for performance-critical components;
Familiarity with workflow orchestration tools (e.g. Airflow or similar);
Experience with embeddings, vector search, or semantic matching;
Background in travel, hospitality, or similar domains.

What success looks like
Clear ownership of the mapping domain from day one;
Significant reduction in manual work within the first 1–2 months;
Stable, reliable pipelines running in production;
Measurable improvement in mapping accuracy over time;
Fast resolution of issues and continuous system improvements.

We offer
Work schedule: full-time;
Duration of the cooperation: Long-term;
Flexible Start: Set your own comfortable working hours that accommodate your individual needs.
Competitive Salary: High standards of remuneration reflecting your contribution and skills.
Vacation: Enjoy 22 days of vacation for full rejuvenation and life enjoyment.
Sick Leave: Ensure your health with 15 days of sick leave per year.
Special Leave Cases: Support for significant life events such as weddings, childbirth, or the loss of a close family member.

