A team that actually ships things, fast;
Mentorship and continuous knowledge exchange;
Access to modern AI tools and platforms;
Clear room to grow — as the field grows, so does the role;
Regular, honest feedback;
Paid time off and sick leaves;
Personalized benefits built around you.

What you need:
A genuine obsession with language, logic, and how models interpret both;
Strong written English — you'll be prompting, documenting, and communicating in it daily;
Understanding of how LLMs work — not theoretically, but practically: context windows, system prompts, temperature, hallucinations, edge cases;
Experience writing and testing prompts across different models (GPT, Claude, Gemini — any);
Structured, analytical thinking — you can break down a vague problem and build a precise solution;
Ability to evaluate outputs critically, not just by "feeling";
