About the Company & Product
We are a rapidly growing product company entering the global gaming entertainment market. Our mission is to bring innovative business solutions to the iGaming industry by developing cutting-edge technology products.

Our core product is a SaaS gaming platform made up of over 200 microservices, delivering a seamless gaming experience to millions of users worldwide. It provides a full suite of iGaming solutions, including game management, payments, analytics, CRM, and more.

We actively scale our B2B direction, we are looking for a Product Owner to help us evolve and scale our platform, drive the development of internal services and modules, and ensure their business value and technical consistency. As a Product Owner, you are responsible for translating product vision and business priorities into a clear, structured, and actionable backlog that the team can confidently deliver.
You act as the single point of entry for requirements into the team, ensuring focus, clarity, and alignment between business goals, product strategy, and technical execution. You work closely with the Product Manager, delivery teams, and stakeholders to maximize product value while maintaining sustainable delivery.

What you’ll be doing
Own and maintain a prioritized, transparent, and outcome-oriented product backlog;
Translate product vision and strategic goals into well-defined user stories with clear acceptance criteria, Definition of Ready (DoR), and Definition of Done (DoD);
Serve as the single source of truth for requirements within the team — filtering incoming requests, removing noise, and preserving focus on high-value work;
Work closely with the Product Manager to align sprint priorities, success metrics, and expected outcomes;
Balance business priorities with technical needs to ensure sustainable product evolution without accumulating technical debt;
Actively participate in sprint ceremonies: refinement, planning, demos, and retrospectives, providing context and clarity to the team;
Ensure the team clearly understands not only what needs to be built, but why it matters for the product and users;
Analyze the impact of delivered features using data (adoption, usage, conversion, error rates) and adjust priorities accordingly;
Communicate status, risks, and expectations clearly to the Product Manager, PMO, and stakeholders;
Foster a collaborative culture with engineering teams, respecting technical expertise and supporting joint decision-making.


You have these superpowers
3+ years of experience as a Product Owner or Business Analyst in a product or delivery team;
Experience in iGaming environment must have (B2B or B2C);
Proven ability to turn product vision and strategy into concrete, deliverable outcomes;
Strong backlog management skills — your backlog is always structured, prioritized, and meaningful;
Ability to explain why a feature matters, not just what needs to be built;
Solid understanding of Agile and Scrum in practice, with experience supporting stable sprint execution;
Experience working with product metrics and understanding how to measure feature success (adoption, usage, conversion, impact);
Strong communication skills and the ability to align business expectations with delivery realities;
Confidence in working with tools such as Jira, Confluence;
Ability to balance user value, business priorities, technical constraints, and realistic delivery scope.


What We Value in a Product Owner
You are a product leader, not just a task manager — you see real business and user value behind every user story;
You translate strategy into action and help the team understand not only what to build, but why;
You are the single gatekeeper of requirements, protecting the team from chaos and constant context switching;
You build trust between product and delivery teams, fostering shared ownership and collaboration;
You understand both business and technology and help find the right balance between value, risks, and technical reality;
You think in data, not assumptions — decisions are driven by results and impact;
You stay fully in context — you know the state of your product, sprint progress, and how each step moves the product toward its goals;
You collaborate closely with the Product Manager and PMO to ensure aligned processes, clear metrics, and a unified delivery system.


How We Measure Success
The backlog is always up-to-date, prioritized, and clearly understood by the team;
Sprint outcomes deliver tangible value that impacts the product and user experience;
Sprint Goals are consistently achieved, and delivery metrics (velocity, completion rate, predictability) remain healthy;
The team understands the context and purpose of their work, resulting in motivated execution without confusion or excessive clarifications;
Communication between product, technical, and delivery functions is aligned, dependencies are managed proactively, and processes run without chaos.0

It’s cool to work with us
Flexible schedule: work from home, the office, or hybrid;
Extra day off for your birthday: take a break any day within the month;
Competitive compensation that matches your skills;
Medical insurance (in Ukraine) and health support;
20 paid vacation days + 15 unpaid vacation days;
22 sick leave days, including mental health days;
Gifts and support for life’s key moments (wedding, childbirth, kindergarten);
Company-provided equipment based on your preferences.


We care about your comfort and help you maintain work-life balance!

