About Us 
We’re building an AI-driven hiring platform designed to transform how organizations evaluate talent. Our product delivers real-time candidate insights, identifies skill gaps, and recommends development pathways - while enabling recruiters to efficiently identify top performers through data-driven decision-making. 

About the Role 
We’re looking for a Psychometrician to join us as a part-time, ongoing consultant. This role combines strategic advisory with hands-on work, ensuring our assessment methodologies are scientifically sound, fair, and compliant with professional and legal standards. 
You’ll collaborate closely with product and engineering to validate and improve our AI-driven assessment systems. 

What You’ll Do 

Evaluate and improve candidate assessment frameworks; 
Design and run validation studies (criterion-related, construct, content validity); 
Establish and monitor reliability metrics (e.g., internal consistency, test-retest); 
Ensure AI-driven scoring aligns with psychometric best practices; 
Audit algorithms for bias, fairness, and adverse impact; 
Support calibration and continuous improvement of ranking models; 
Ensure alignment with EEOC, APA, and SIOP standards; 
Conduct adverse impact analyses and assess subgroup differences;  
Recommend and implement bias mitigation strategies; 
Define and track key measurement KPIs (validity, reliability, fairness); 
Translate technical findings into clear, actionable insights; 
Prepare documentation for audits, certification, and external validation. 

Success Metrics 
Assessment validity and reliability clearly established and documented; 
Fairness and bias benchmarks defined, tracked, and improved over time; 
Readiness for certification or third-party validation within agreed timelines. 
Core Requirements 

Master’s or PhD in Psychometrics, Industrial-Organizational Psychology, Statistics, or a related field; 
5+ years of experience in assessment validation, ideally in hiring or talent assessment; 
Strong knowledge of Item Response Theory (IRT) and/or Classical Test Theory (CTT); 
Experience designing and executing validation studies; 
Hands-on experience with adverse impact and fairness analysis; 
Strong analytical and problem-solving skills; 
Ability to work independently in a remote, flexible environment; 
Clear communication skills, especially with non-technical stakeholders. 
Nice to Have 

Experience with AI/ML-based hiring or assessment systems;  
Background in HR tech or talent analytics; 
Experience supporting audits, certification, or compliance processes;  
Academic or research affiliation. 
Engagement Details 

Part-time, ongoing consulting role; 
Fully remote with flexible hours; 
Mix of strategic advisory and hands-on work.

