About the Role:
You will be joining a team building a secure, privacy-focused communication platform designed for organisations where data protection, control, and regulatory compliance are mission critical. The product provides encrypted messaging, voice, and video communication built on a zero-trust security architecture with strong end-to-end encryption. It supports flexible deployment models — including on-premise and controlled cloud environments — and is used by security-sensitive and regulated organisations to protect confidential communications and maintain full data sovereignty.
As a QA Automation Engineer, you will be responsible for building and maintaining automated test coverage across iOS and Android, ensuring the reliability and integrity of features where quality is not just a standard — it is a compliance requirement.
What You Will Work On:
Designing, writing, and maintaining automated test suites for iOS and Android mobile applications using Appium and Java;
Covering encrypted messaging, voice/video calling, file sharing, and meeting features with automated scenarios;
Developing and maintaining test frameworks and reporting pipelines with TestNG and Allure;
Integrating automated tests into CI/CD workflows via GitLab pipelines;
Managing test cases and documentation in Testiny; tracking defects in Jira;
Collaborating with developers and product managers throughout the full QA cycle;
Leveraging Claude for AI-assisted test generation and QA workflow optimization.
Required Skills:
At least 6 months of hands-on experience in mobile test automation for iOS and Android applications
Hands-on experience with Appium for mobile test automation;
Proficiency in Java for writing and maintaining automated test scripts;
Experience with TestNG as a test framework;
Allure for test reporting and result visualization;
Jira for bug tracking and task management;
Testiny for test case management;
GitLab - CI/CD pipelines, MR workflows, test integration;
Claude - AI-assisted tooling in QA workflows;
English level: Intermediate+ or higher (written and spoken).
Nice to Have:
Experience testing security-sensitive, privacy-focused, or compliance-driven products (HIPAA, GDPR, ISO 27001, etc.);
Familiarity with zero-trust security concepts or end-to-end encryption;
Experience testing real-time communication features: VoIP, video calls, WebRTC;
Basic API automation skills (REST Assured or similar);
Understanding of cross-device and cross-platform compatibility testing strategies.
Tech Stack:
Appium · Java · TestNG · Allure · Jira · Testiny · GitLab · Claude

