About the Client
Our client is building advanced spatial computing and AI-powered solutions that transform large-scale visual data into accurate, high-quality 3D models. Their platform leverages cutting-edge computer vision, cloud infrastructure, and emerging technologies to solve complex real-world problems across industries.

About the Role
We are looking for a Senior Computer Vision & Photogrammetry Engineer to join the client’s team. This is a senior, high-impact role for someone who can bridge deep algorithmic expertise with scalable, production-grade infrastructure.
You will lead the design and deployment of high-performance 3D reconstruction pipelines, working closely with engineering and infrastructure teams to turn massive datasets into precise spatial outputs.
​
What You’ll Do

Design and implement photogrammetry pipelines, including Structure from Motion (SfM), Multi-View Stereo (MVS), and bundle adjustment;

Build and optimize high-performance 3D reconstruction workflows for large-scale datasets;

Architect and manage compute infrastructure using Docker and Kubernetes;

Develop data processing pipelines for ingesting, cleaning, and analyzing image and sensor data;

Optimize algorithms for accuracy, performance, and scalability in production environments;

Integrate multi-sensor data (e.g., IMU, GPS, LiDAR) for improved spatial accuracy;

Apply state estimation techniques such as Kalman Filters for sensor fusion;

Explore and integrate emerging approaches like Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) and Gaussian Splatting;

Optimize cloud-based processing workflows, particularly within AWS environments;

Collaborate with cross-functional teams to productionize research-driven solutions;

Monitor and improve system performance, reliability, and cost efficiency;

Contribute to technical direction and best practices across computer vision and infrastructure.

Core Requirements

7+ years of experience in computer vision, photogrammetry, or spatial data engineering;

Strong programming expertise in Python, including data processing with Pandas;

Deep understanding of 3D geometry, camera models, and coordinate transformations;

Proven experience with Structure from Motion (SfM) and Multi-View Stereo (MVS) pipelines;

Strong experience with Docker and Kubernetes in production environments;

Hands-on experience with large-scale data processing and optimization;

Experience with at least one key 3D/vision library (e.g., Open3D, PCL, or Ceres Solver);

Strong problem-solving skills and ability to work on complex technical systems;

Nice to Have

Experience with SLAM (Simultaneous Localization and Mapping);

Practical experience with NeRF or Gaussian Splatting;

Experience implementing Kalman Filters or similar estimation techniques;

Strong AWS experience (EC2 GPU, S3, Lambda, Batch, SageMaker);

Background in real-time systems or sensor fusion;

Experience with Kotlin.

What We Offer

Competitive market salary;

Fully remote work;

Flexible working hours with overlap requirements;

28 days of paid time off per calendar year;

Opportunity to work on impactful, cutting-edge technology;

Collaboration with a highly professional, international team;

Challenging projects with strong opportunities for growth and learning.

Success Metrics

High-performance, scalable 3D reconstruction pipelines deployed to production;

Measurable improvements in model accuracy and processing efficiency;

Reliable and cost-optimized cloud infrastructure;

Successful integration of advanced techniques into production workflows.
